diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 4479b53..23d5a52 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -2,6 +2,36 @@
 
 This project is a sample news application built with Astro, designed to serve as a testing ground for new features in Chrome DevTools.
 
+## Phone verification during sign-up
+
+Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and supply server-only `TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID`,
+`TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN`, and `TWILIO_MESSAGING_SERVICE_SID` values. The Messaging Service
+must have an SMS-capable sender. Set `SIGNUP_ORIGIN` to the exact public origin
+(for example `https://news.example.com`, without `/devtools-times/` or a trailing
+slash). Deploy behind HTTPS for WebOTP. Twilio trial accounts can send only to
+verified recipients. Delivery uses the [Twilio Messages API](https://www.twilio.com/docs/messaging/api/message-resource).
+
+The form sends a six-digit code before account creation. A cryptographically random
+code is hashed with a random salt in the server session, expires after five minutes,
+allows five attempts, and is consumed before registration. Resending replaces the
+old code; requests have a 60-second cooldown and a limit of five per session per hour.
+Passwords and plaintext codes are never stored in the session. Keep session storage
+private and shared across instances when deploying more than one server.
+
+Messages end with `@<SIGNUP_ORIGIN hostname> #<code>` on the last line for origin-bound
+WebOTP extraction and keyboard autofill. The browser starts listening before SMS
+delivery and cancels on submission, resend, changing details, or unmount. Browsers
+without WebOTP can still use keyboard suggestions, paste, or manual numeric entry.
+Provider errors are shown without exposing credentials or verification codes.
+
+The same-origin `api/signup` endpoint checks the code before calling the existing
+external registration service. The external service must also restrict direct
+registration if phone verification is to be mandatory for **all** API clients; this
+repository cannot change that separately hosted service. The `phone` field is sent
+with registration, but persisting it depends on the external service's schema.
+Add provider/edge limits by recipient and IP before exposing SMS delivery to broad
+traffic; session limits alone do not stop clients that repeatedly clear cookies.
+
 
 ```sh
 pnpm install && pnpm run start
